on the third day of digging  police were said to have uncovered a  hidden cellar they hoped it would  provide the crucial evidence they need  sniffer dogs joined the search in the  garden of a secluded holiday chalet  where the suspect once lived  police were hunting for clues to the  disappearance of madeleine mccann  clinton  officers sifted piles of soil dug from a  hole  15 meters wide they also used ground  penetrating radar and later brought in a  drone  [Music]  three skips were removed not all of them  full drifter christian b is the main  suspect  in what the german prosecutor calls a  murder investigation  madeleine vanished 13 years ago during a  holiday in portugal  the suspect was living there at the time  soon after madeleine disappeared  the suspect moved here one police theory  is  he drove her with him on a journey of  more than 24 hours  [Music]  question it's difficult to judge the  importance of this search  it's wide seemingly unfocused  perhaps even a fishing expedition in a  location that police have known about  for three years but they wouldn't  normally  spend such time effort and resources if  they didn't have credible information  that they're likely to find vital  evidence here  police wouldn't say if they'd found any  evidence or whether they're to search  anywhere else martin brunt sky news  hanover
 

